.TH CUBBY 1 "2026" "cubby 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cubby \- left-edge dock with one workspace per app
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cubby
[\fB\-\-width\fR \fIPX\fR] [\fB\-\-icon\fR \fIPX\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-respect\-top\fR] [\fB\-\-respect\-bottom\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cubby
is a dock for X11 desktops. Each application is moved to its own workspace and
gets a button in the dock; clicking the button switches to that workspace.
The dock also has an app drawer, pinned apps and folders, a network indicator,
a clock with calendar and a user menu.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-width " PX"
Dock width.
.TP
.BI \-\-icon " PX"
Icon size.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Config file. Default: \fI~/.config/cubby/dock.json\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-respect\-top
Start below existing top panels instead of at the top of the screen.
.TP
.B \-\-respect\-bottom
End above existing bottom panels instead of at the bottom of the screen.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/cubby/dock.json
Pins, folders, panel options and per\-app workspace settings.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/cubby/examples/cubby\-autostart.desktop
Example autostart entry; copy it to \fI~/.config/autostart/\fR.
.SH NOTES
Requires an X11 session with an EWMH\-compliant window manager. It does not
work on Wayland.
.SH AUTHOR
Jordan Webb.
